@_thomasip yea i get what you mean - i worked in a team of 11 engineers and was the only female 😅

i think it’s a mix of structural factors and self selection. there’s bias in what skills are encouraged and narratives around what technical careers; people are more inclined to be in a space where they feel they belong 

i remember reading research showing that girls in mixed schools rated their math ability lower than girls in single sex schools, even when their actual performance was similar

@davidbmadsen most tools available are built for enterprise

$50-100+ per month, with many extra features indie devs won’t need

rankd is a streamlined tool that shows the data + steps that matter

@Bill03_Dev - find 10-15 bigger accounts with content similar to what you’d like to post, and study their tweets 

- write your posts in the same structure and hook, but with your own content

- reply to 10-20 accounts everyday, ideally the same accounts so it creates familiarity and genuine connection
